<h2>What JSON formatting changes</h2><p>Pretty-printing changes whitespace and indentation but not the parsed data structure. Minifying removes unnecessary formatting whitespace to make the JSON string more compact.</p><h2>How to use this tool</h2><ol><li>Paste a JSON document into the input field.</li><li>Choose Format for readable two-space indentation or Minify for compact output.</li><li>If parsing fails, use the browser's error message to find the syntax problem.</li><li>Copy the corrected output when valid.</li></ol><h2>Common JSON syntax mistakes</h2><p>JSON requires double-quoted property names and string values, does not allow trailing commas, and uses <code>true</code>, <code>false</code> and <code>null</code> as lowercase literals.</p><h2>Local processing</h2><p>This version uses the browser's built-in JSON parser. Input is not intentionally sent to a ToolboxKart server by the formatter.</p>
